Route Node (IBM Integration Toolkit)

Last Updated: 2023-06-21
Used for: Directing messages to different paths in a message flow based on specific criteria.


---

Operation Modes Available In

Developer

Application Integration Suite

Standard

Advanced

Scale



---

Purpose

Route messages based on XPath filter expressions.

Bypass unnecessary steps (e.g., skip DB lookup if data is present).

Trigger multiple events using Distribution Mode = All.

Example: Log by account ID or audit by product.



---

XPath Filters

Use XPath 1.0.

Filters return Boolean (true / false).

Example filter:

$Root/XMLNSC/EmployeeRecord/EmployeeNumber="00001"



---

Message Flow Structure

Terminals: | Terminal | Type | Purpose | |----------|------|---------| | In | Static | Receives message | | Match | Dynamic | Routed if expression is true | | Default | Static | If no match | | Failure | Static | If an error occurs |

Dynamic Terminals: Can define multiple. Unmapped ones won’t receive messages.



